    Rate limit Alogs
        Token Bucket - Token bucket is a container with pre defined capacity. Every time interval certain
            amount of tokens are added. When a request comes , a token is taken out. If not token , request rejected
                Two params : Bucket Size , Refill Rate - No of tokens put into bucket every second
                No of buckets depends upon use case.

                Pros : Easy Algo , Memory Efficient ,
                Cons: Two params . hard to tune both

        Leaking Bucket :
            Similar to token bucket. But instead of Bucket a queue is used. A request is added to queue
            and pulled from queue at regular interval.
            Two Params : Bucket Size/Queue Size , Outflow rate - how many requests can be processed in a second

            Pros : Memory efficient with limited queue size  , requests are processed at a fixed rate .
                suitable for use cases that a stable outflow needed

             Cons: Burst traffic fills up the queue ... if not processed.. recent requests will be rate limited..
                    two parmas hard to tune

        Fixed Window Counter
        timeline divided into fix sized time window and assigned a counter for each window..
        requests increment the count.. once threshold is reached..requests are rejected...till a new window stast
            Fixed time window with
            Edge bursts could cause more requests to drop
        Sliding window log
                keeps log of every request time stamp.. rolls time window.. once new request comes ... all outdated
                requests are removed from the window.. a new request added.. till the allowed limit

                    Say size is 2. Request is 1:00:01 and 1:00:30 .. allowed.. 1:00:50 rejected.. a new request comes ay
                        1:1:40 allowed n window become 1:0:40 1:14:... olderer requests before 1:0:40 are rejected

                        Works like charm by memory inefficient
        Sliding window counter
            is hybrid approacj fixed window count and sliding window log
                Requests in current window + previous window*overlap percentage - at a time


